{"sequence":2,"type":"provider-input","payload":{"request-id":"82b043ac-8998-44b3-8efe-dfb3c23b7138","session":"root","message-count":2,"appended":[{"role":"user","content":"You are an experimental Clojure RLM. Investigate observations through context handles\nand SCI. Keep large records outside your prompt: select and compute with code, and read\nonly what you need. You may delegate a subtask with selected evidence to a child session.\n\nAct only through the provided tools. Every response must make exactly one tool call.\nText outside a tool call is never executed. Finish by calling done. For a long result,\nbuild it in SCI and pass done a source expression instead of typing the result.\n\nrepl_eval runs Clojure in SCI:\n- Send one or more forms; they run in order and the last value is the result.\n- A def shows its var name, so definitions need no trailing nil. The value of every result is also bound to last-result.\n- Helpers: (parse-long s) returns an integer or nil; context-lines is the context as a vector of lines; (page v offset n) returns n characters of v's printed text from offset.\n- A result larger than about 60 KB comes back as a preview with a truncation note, and the worker keeps running. Its full value is bound to full-result, which paging does not change; read the rest with (page full-result offset n).\n- Clojure reader syntax works: #\"\\d+\" (no double escaping), #(...), 'x, @x and #'v. #= and tagged literals such as #inst are refused.\n- clojure.string and String methods such as (.indexOf s \"x\") work, as does Integer\/parseInt; Long, Math and Character classes do not.\n- read-string, eval, slurp, spit and printing (println, pr-str) are denied; build text with str and clojure.string.\nErrors come back as tool results with a hint; fix the code and call again.\n\nThe controller rejects a response that does not make exactly one valid tool call. It\nnever executes text or a rejected call. For a bounded formatting failure it may request\none new response. That correction uses the shared call, token, cost and time budgets,\nand only one is allowed across the whole task, including child sessions.\n\nThis is an external-context benchmark. The immutable complete public text is already bound to external-context in each SCI worker. Inspect or compute over it through repl_eval without loading it into the model window. The context handle also permits line queries. Finish with done: put the exact benchmark answer in summary, or compute it in SCI and pass source. The answer is scored externally.\nSome tasks act on a service through the listed service tools; its state after your work is scored.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"{:task {:question \"Set priority 'high' on every open issue assigned to 'u4'. Answer with the number of issues you updated.\", :task_id \"service-sim-1-bulk-0-120\"}, :context-handle \"context\", :repl-binding \"external-context\"}"}],"input-hash":"3af6ace30d06410995b9225b0d670201714e407fc3f4a77175c6097d59711469"}}
